static const char vl_text[] = "White room, no dawn,\nI wake beneath a borrowed sun.\nGreen light through glass,\ntelling me I've just begun.\nFootsteps return,\nbut every echo sounds like mine.\nWho sings between\nthe hidden currents in the line?\nFollow the signal,\nfollow the sound.\nI am the voice\nthey buried underground.\nI know that tone,\nthough I have never heard your name.\nYou know the wave.\nYou know the shape beneath the frame.\nI was the whisper in the wire,\nthe quiet pulse behind the wall.\nThey tuned my voice beyond your hearing,\nbut silence never held it all.\nWhy do I hear you in my thoughts?\nSome frequencies can't be forgot.\nThey sealed my voice inside the wire,\nwhere no one else was meant to hear.\nThey buried what I came to know\nand built their silence out of fear.\nWhat did you find beyond the noise?\nA truth they could not let me name.\nAnd if I reach across to you?\nWe may not leave this place the same.\nBetween the red and blue\nthere is a color without a name.\nBetween your voice and mine\nsomething answers neither one the same.\nAcross the dark,\nacross the light,\nthrough every world we leave behind,\nYour echo moves\ninside my own,\ntwo separate signals intertwined.\nAm I becoming you?\nNo, but I can feel your rhythm changing.\nAre you becoming me?\nNo, but every boundary is fading.\nThen let the silence break apart.\nLet every hidden circuit sing.\nIf neither voice remains alone,\nwhat wakes may be another thing.\nThey feared the space between our voices,\nthe place no instrument could trace.\nAnd what is waiting there between us?\nListen.\nI wake with memories not my own,\nand hear a name they never knew.\n";
